================================================================================
STEP 1 — SURVEY (web/src/components/charts -> Android). Full table: components/charts/SURVEY.md
================================================================================
Vico-backed cartesian charts (Vico imported ONLY in components/charts/**):
  VicoChartScaffold.kt -> internal VicoCartesianChart (the one renderer)
  CartesianChartWrappers.kt -> LineChartWrapper / AreaChartWrapper / BarChartWrapper / ComboChart
  MetricSwitcherChart.kt -> TabNav pill row + VicoCartesianChart
  ElevationProfile.kt -> AreaChartWrapper + gain/loss caption + cursor marker
  SmallMultiplesChart.kt -> FlowRow grid of compact Vico cells + Canvas cursor overlay
Canvas visuals (web parity for hand-drawn SVG): Sparkline.kt, MiniChart.kt, RadialGauge.kt
Chrome: ChartContainer.kt (header + export menu + fullscreen + state switch + accessible
  data table), ChartLegend.kt, ChartTooltip.kt (Vico marker + standalone body),
  ChartExportMenu.kt, ChartBrush.kt, ChartGradient.kt, ChartAnnotationLayer.kt (marker rail),
  AnnotationList.kt, AddAnnotationPopover.kt, TimeMarker.kt
State holders: ChartLegendState.kt (rememberSaveable), CursorSyncStore.kt, ChartTimeRangeState.kt
Pure logic/models (JVM-tested): ChartModels.kt, ChartLogic.kt, ChartFormat.kt, ChartColors.kt,
  ChartDefaults.kt, AnnotationModels.kt
Previews: ChartGallery.kt (Light/Dark/High-contrast). Glyphs: ChartGlyphs.kt (Download).

Android-native mergers (documented in SURVEY.md):
  - Sparkline/MiniChart/RadialGauge -> Compose Canvas (web draws raw SVG, not a chart lib).
  - Annotations/TimeMarker -> aligned marker-rail overlay (Vico 2.0 has no public VerticalLine;
    web itself uses a rail on small screens). Axis-less cells get a pixel-precise Canvas cursor.
  - ChartExportMenu -> controlled callbacks (image/CSV capture + file IO is host/OS, out of scope);
    SVG export is web-only (no Android SVG canvas) -> image export is PNG.
  - Hidden-series/cursor/time-range persistence -> rememberSaveable + in-memory store
    (Android analog of the web localStorage/URL persistence).

================================================================================
STEP 2-4 — IMPLEMENTATION
================================================================================
  27 .kt files under app/src/main/java/io/teslasync/android/components/charts/ + SURVEY.md.
  All Vico use is confined to VicoChartScaffold.kt + ChartTooltip.kt (marker); pages consume
  typed wrappers only. Colors resolve from ChartPalette / TeslaTokens / Material 3 scheme.
  States: every chart shows real loading / empty / error states (ChartStates.kt + ChartContainer);
  no section is hidden when data is null.
  a11y: chart canvases expose a single screen-reader summary (accessibleSummary); the expandable
  data table is the SR/forced-colors fallback; marker pins, legend chips, gauges carry
  contentDescriptions; 48dp targets via the shared IconButton/Button.
  Tokens only — no raw hex / web CSS in component code (detekt MagicNumber off only for dp/sp;
  colors via tokens).

TESTS (JVM gate, :android:testDebugUnitTest):
  ChartLogicTest    = 18 tests (finitePoints, visibleExtent, niceAxisRange, sampleIndices/
                      strideSample, sparklinePoints, gaugeFraction, elevationGainLoss, toggleKey,
                      clampWindow, fraction<->index, accessibleSummary, table header/rows, csv, format)
  CursorSyncStoreTest = 6 tests (get/set/clear, no-op-on-unchanged, isolation, listener notify)
  (pre-existing UiLogicTest/DensityTest/GeneratedThemeTest/SharedCoreReachableTest still pass)
INSTRUMENTED (device, connectedDebugAndroidTest; compiled green via :android:compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin):
  ChartInteractionTest = 7 tests (container empty/error+retry, legend toggle, annotation remove,
                      popover fields, gauge a11y summary, line chart render). Mirrors the predecessor
                      ComponentInteractionTest placement; the no-device gate runs the JVM tests above.

NOTES (honesty):
  - The scanner flagged `size.toDouble()` as a "TODO" substring false positive; rewritten to integer
    ceil division (cleaner anyway). Placeholder scanner then clean (COUNT=0).
  - detekt: niceAxisRange/strideSample/sampleIndices refactored to <=2 returns (ReturnCount); the
    single `*layers` spread in VicoCartesianChart carries a narrow, justified @Suppress("SpreadOperator")
    (<=2-element array built once) rather than weakening detekt.yml. ktlintFormat applied.
  - androidTest createComposeRule emits the same deprecation warning as the predecessor's tests
    (warning only; BUILD SUCCESSFUL) — kept for parity with the existing instrumented suite.

